    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10064": {
      "title": "Student Mail Clerk",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Student Mail Clerk Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Mail Clerk Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Student Mail Clerk Department Central Receiving Rate of Pay $8.00 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week 10-12 Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Work-Study General Description Sort, deliver, and box mail and packages. Essential Job Duties 1. Retrieve and deliver mail from and to the city post office. 2. Sort and prepare mail to put in PO Boxes. 3. Run campus mail route to select University offices; retrieving out-going and delivering in-coming mail. 4. Weigh and apply appropriate postage to out-going mail, daily. 5. Perform light cleaning and organizing duties in Post Office and mail delivery vehicle. 6. Sell stamps and be able to make change. 7. Make sure appropriate amount of stamps is applied to outgoing mail. 8. Distribute Post Office box combinations to new and returning students. 9. Help customers with mailboxes and mailing questions. 10. Sign for packages. 11. Distribute packages to correct recipients. 12. Reconcile stamp/cash drawer. 13. Perform light filing alphabetically and numerically. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 1. A drivers license with a good driving record is a plus. 2. Must have ability to lift up to 50 pounds on occasion. 3. Ability to briefly tolerate outdoor weather (i.e. rain, cold, heat, etc.). 4. Good customer service skills. 5. Ability to learn to operate postage meter. 6. Ability to work independently and stay on task and schedule. 7. Knowledge of basic postage procedures preferred. 8. Knowledge of University Departments and their locations preferred. 9. Ability to read and sort mail packages by department and box number. 10. Ability to follow Post Office procedures and make rational decisions. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations Valid drivers license. Meet the successful completion of a MVR check. Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date 08/20/2025 Open Date 08/13/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. 