      "title": "Student Technical Support Staff",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Student Technical Support Staff Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Technical Support Staff Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Student Technical Support Staff Department University Events and Calendar Office Rate of Pay $8.75 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week 10 Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Jobship and Work-Study General Description Assist with technical aspects of setup, break down, and coordination of University events as well as host off-campus groups. Essential Job Duties 1. Assist with setup and break down of audio and visual equipment: i.e., public address systems, projectors, and screens: including analog and digital equipment. 2. Test audio and visual equipment prior to events and troubleshoot and resolve problems. 3. Set-up staging, flooring, tables and chairs for events. 4. Act as an official host at University events. 5. Dress and gaff cables for best aesthetic and technical presentations. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 1. Basic knowledge of analog and digital audio and visual equipment is highly preferred. 2. Must have ability to distinguish quality sound and EQ sound equipment for optimum experience for event attenders. 3. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds. 4. Position requires bending, stooping, and reaching to lay cables. 5. Ability to follow instructions and work well in a team environment. 6. Flexible schedule permitting evening and weekend work. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations N/A Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 08/19/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Class Schedule Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
