    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10088": {
      "title": "Data Analytics - Student Assistant",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Data Analytics - Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Data Analytics - Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Data Analytics - Student Assistant Department Stephens College of Business Rate of Pay $12.00 - $18.00 FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week 10-12 Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Jobship General Description Join a pioneering experiential learning initiative designed to solve real-world challenges for our community and campus partners. This project provides students in data-focused fields with a unique opportunity to apply their classroom knowledge to impactful projects, develop in-demand professional skills, and build a powerful portfolio. You will be hired as a Student Data Analyst and matched to a specific project based on your skills and interests, working with community partners. Pay Rate: $12 – $18 per hour Duration: 34 weeks (Academic Year: Fall and Spring Semesters) Hours: 10-12 hours per week Location: Stephens College of Business Supervisor: Dr. Shafqat Ali Shad & Dr. Carolyn Garrity Essential Job Duties As a Student Data Analyst, you will be responsible for a full analytics lifecycle on a dedicated project. Your duties will include: Collaboration: Meeting with a community or campus partner to understand their business challenges and data needs. Data Wrangling: Identifying, collecting, cleaning, and managing data from various primary and secondary sources. Analysis & Modeling: Performing statistical analysis, identifying trends, and building models to generate actionable insights. Data Visualization: Creating clear and compelling charts, graphs, and interactive dashboards (using tools like Tableau, Power BI, or Excel) to communicate findings. Storytelling: Synthesizing your analysis into formal reports and presentations to provide data-driven recommendations to stakeholders. Project Management: Managing your time effectively to meet project milestones and deadlines. Education and Experience Current UM students Major/Minor in Data Analytics or Minor in Cybersecurity or Business Major who already completed QM237 & QM238 Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Skills & Knowledge Successful completion of introductory courses in data, statistics, or programming. Proficiency with Microsoft Excel for data analysis (e.g., PivotTables, formulas). and Python Strong intellectual curiosity, problem-solving skills, and a desire to learn. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and manage time effectively across a long-term project. Preferred Skills & Knowledge Experience with one or more of the following: SQL , Python, R, Tableau, Power BI, or Google Analytics. Experience working on a team-based project (academic or professional). A strong academic record. Preferred Major Data Analytics,  Cybersecurity, or Marketing Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Required Number of Vacancies 4 Desired Start Date 09/19/2025 Open Date 09/19/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/9961": {
      "title": "Student Office Assistant, Human Resources",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Student Office Assistant, Human Resources Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Office Assistant, Human Resources Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Student Office Assistant, Human Resources Department Human Resources Rate of Pay $8 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Work-Study General Description The purpose of this position is to provide office administrative support for Human Resources. Essential Job Duties 1) Provide friendly and helpful customer service by welcoming and assisting visitors in the HR Office. 2) Answer phones, direct calls, and take accurate phone messages. 3) Organize information and file a large volume of documents. 4) Organize and inventory office supplies. 5) Assist with departmental events and programs as necessary. 6) Make Xerox copies and assemble information packets. 7) Run errands across campus. 8) Perform other duties as assigned. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 1) Be self-directed and motivated. 2) Adhere to strict ethical and legal requirements concerning confidentiality and protecting information. 3) Must be detail oriented. 4) Ability to interact with HR patrons in a positive and effective way. 5) Dress appropriately for a professional setting. 6) Ability to use office equipment (Xerox Copier, Facsimile, and Multi-line Phone system). Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 07/04/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Letter of Application Resume University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
