    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10498": {
      "title": "Falcon Success Center Student Office Assistant",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Falcon Success Center Student Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Falcon Success Center Student Office Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Falcon Success Center Student Office Assistant Department Falcon Success Center Rate of Pay $8.00 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Jobship and Work-Study General Description The purpose of this position is to provide office support for the Falcon Success Center. Essential Job Duties 1. Answering phone calls and taking messages, helping the callers, or transferring calls. 2. Checking and replying to e-mails. 3. Greeting students, faculty, and staff as they enter the FSC and acting as a liaison between guests and FSC staff. 4. Enter data into various computer programs. 5. Running errands on campus as needed. 6. Assisting with marketing efforts on campus and through social media outlets. 7. Assisting with events in the FSC and for the FSC around campus. 8. Assisting in other areas as needed. 9. Scheduling tutoring and success coaching appointments for students. 10. Checking in students present for appointments and introducing them to their tutor/success coach. 11. Maintaining the Falcon Success Center space by wiping surfaces and keeping the ground floor of the library tidy. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 1. Be self-directed and motivated. 2. Adhere to strict ethical and legal requirements concerning confidentiality and protecting information. 3. Must be detail oriented and able to multitask. 4. Ability to interact with students, faculty, and staff in a positive and effective way. 5. Proficient in Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook. 6. Must have excellent written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 08/26/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
