    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10526": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Counseling (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, Counseling (Tenure-Track) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor, Counseling (Tenure-Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500148 Job Title Assistant Professor, Counseling (Tenure-Track) Position Number TBD Salary Commensurate with experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Tenure Track General Description The University of Montevallo invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Counseling position specializing in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. This faculty member will contribute to our CACREP -accredited program by teaching, supervising, conducting research, and engaging in service to the university and profession. Essential Job Duties Teach graduate-level courses in core CACREP and Clinical Mental Health Counseling specialization areas. · Provide academic advising to graduate students. · Supervise graduate student field placements (practicum/internship). · Maintain an independent research agenda and engage in scholarly activities (e.g., publish in peer-reviewed journals, deliver professional presentations). · Engage in professional counseling organizations and demonstrate active professional identity (e.g., ACA , AMHCA , ALCA ). · Actively recruit graduate students and contribute to program growth. · Serve on university, college, and department committees and contribute to the broader counseling community. Additional Duties Education and Experience Doctorate in Counselor Education from a CACREP -accredited program (or related doctoral degree with one full-time faculty year before July 1, 2013). · University-level teaching experience in counseling. · Education and clinical experience in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. · Active professional engagement, including at least two of the following: Professional development in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. Professional service/advocacy in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. Ongoing clinical practice. Research/scholarly activity in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. · Professional counseling identity demonstrated through: o Membership in national and state counseling organizations (e.g., ACA , AMHCA , ALCA ). Relevant professional credentials (e.g., LPC , NCC ). Preferred Education and Experience Established research agenda in counselor education. Experience in securing external funding for academic research. Demonstrated leadership in graduate counseling education. Licenses, Certification or Registrations Candidates must hold or be eligible for counseling licensure as an LPC in Alabama within 18 months of hire. Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Open Date 09/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information Required documents: Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application Other document: Proof of License Unofficial Transcripts Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10508 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10525": {
      "title": "Open-Rank, Tenure-Track Faculty in Counseling",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Open-Rank, Tenure-Track Faculty in Counseling – Director, Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Open-Rank, Tenure-Track Faculty in Counseling – Director, Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500149 Job Title Open-Rank, Tenure-Track Faculty in Counseling – Director, Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic Position Number TBD Salary Commensurate with experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Tenure Track General Description The University of Montevallo invites applications for an open-rank, tenure-track faculty position in Counseling. The successful candidate will teach in the Graduate Counseling Program and serve as Director of the Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic, the program’s on-campus training clinic. Responsibilities include teaching graduate counseling courses, providing leadership and oversight of clinic operations, providing site supervision to practicum and internship students completing clinical experiences within the clinic, supervising graduate assistants assigned to the clinic, and coordinating clinic-related community outreach initiatives. The position carries a 2/2 teaching load in recognition of the faculty member’s assigned Clinic Director and clinical supervision responsibilities. The faculty member will also receive a separate contract for clinic operations during the summer outside of the 9-month base contract period. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Essential Job Duties Teach graduate-level courses in the Counseling Program with a 2/2 course load, reflecting assigned responsibilities as Director of the program’s on-campus training clinic. Serve as Director of the Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic and provide leadership and oversight of the clinic’s operations, clinical training activities, and community services. Provide site supervision for practicum and internship students completing clinical experiences within the Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic, consistent with program, university, accreditation, and professional standards. Supervise graduate assistants assigned to the Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic. Provide academic advising and mentorship to graduate students in the Counseling Program. Maintain an active program of scholarship, including peer-reviewed publications and professional presentations. Maintain an active professional counseling identity through engagement in relevant professional organizations and activities. Participate in recruitment, retention, and other initiatives that support the continued growth and success of the Counseling Program. Serve on department, college, and university committees and contribute service to the counseling profession and broader community. Perform other duties consistent with the faculty role and the needs of the Counseling Program. Additional Duties Perform other duties as assigned that are consistent with the faculty member’s role, academic appointment, and responsibilities within the Counseling Program and Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic. Participate in additional program, department, college, or university initiatives as appropriate to the faculty role. Education and Experience Doctorate in Counselor Education from a CACREP -accredited program (or related doctoral degree with one full-time faculty year before July 1, 2013). · Demonstrated professional identity and active engagement in the counseling profession, including at least two of the following: Participation in counseling-related continuing education, conferences, workshops, or other professional development activities. Professional service, leadership, or advocacy in counseling. Ongoing clinical practice or clinical supervision. Research, scholarship, presentations, or publications in counseling or counselor education. Preferred Education and Experience Graduate-level teaching experience in counseling or counselor education. · Experience with the administration, coordination, or operation of a university-based counseling training clinic or comparable clinical training environment. · Experience supervising and supporting the clinical development of graduate counseling students. Experience with CACREP -accredited counseling programs and clinical training standards. · Supervision-related credentials (e.g., LPC -S, LMFT -S, ACS ) or equivalent state-recognized supervision credential. Licenses, Certification or Registrations Candidates must hold and maintain an active, independent professional license in counseling or marriage and family therapy (e.g., LPC , LMFT , or equivalent) in a U.S. state or jurisdiction. Candidates must maintain appropriate professional licensure throughout their appointment consistent with accreditation requirements and assigned clinical supervision responsibilities. Eligibility for licensure as an LPC or LMFT in Alabama is preferred. Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Open Date 09/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information Required documents: Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application Other document: Proof of License Unofficial Transcripts Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10510 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application Other Document Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10528": {
      "title": "Assistant Supervisor, Custodial Services",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Assistant Supervisor, Custodial Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Supervisor, Custodial Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S1500769 Job Title Assistant Supervisor, Custodial Services Position Number C14723 Division President - PRS Department Custodial Services FLSA Non-Exempt Salary Grade 111 Salary Classification Classified Annual Salary Range Hourly Salary Range $14.47 - $19.30 Employment Status Full Time 12 Mos Regular General Description The purpose of this position is to assist with supervision of custodial services and daily operations of the department. Plan, develop, organize, and direct all aspects of custodial services. Essential Job Duties Clean and maintain assigned areas Use Flowpath software to enter, assign, and complete work orders as needed. Train new custodial staff Inspect buildings and work areas to ensure cleanliness, sanitation, and maintenance standards are met. Assist with employees’ schedules, attendance records, and coverage for absences. Maintain records, complete inspection reports, and communicate operational issues to supervisor. Assist with special events, after-hour emergencies, and deep cleaning projects. Clean carpet as needed. Performs supervisor duties in their absence. Essential job duties are intended to be examples of duties and are not intended to be all inclusive. There will be other duties as assigned. The individual holding this position will serve as a representative of the University and, as such, shall promote a positive impression by demonstrating a collegial and professional customer-service approach at all times. Additional Duties None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Proficient in Microsoft office (Word, Excel, Outlook) Email and calendar management Basic inventory and supply tracking Printing, scanning, and document management. Knowledge of facilities and campus layout; Ability to delegate and manage workloads; Ability to work safely with chemicals and equipment; Excellent customer service skills; Ability to communicate effectively both oral and written; Ability to work on-call and before/after normal work hours as requested. Education and Experience The educational requirement for this position is: High School diploma/ GED Education substituted for experience? No This position requires: 4 years of related experience. Experience substituted for education? No Licenses, Certification or Registrations The educational requirement for this position is: High School diploma/ GED Education substituted for experience? No This position requires: 4 years of related experience. Experience substituted for education? No Environmental Working Conditions Indoor and Outdoor Travel Requirements None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Physical Requirements The physical activities required for this position involve: Standing: Over 2/3 of the time; walking: Over 2/3 of the time; sitting: Under 1/3 of the time; using hands: Up to 2/3 of the time; reaching with hands and arms: Up to 2/3 of the time; climbing or balancing: Up to 2/3 of the time; stooping, kneeling, crouching, or crawling: Up to 2/3 of the time; talking or hearing: Over 2/3 of the time. This position requires lifting: Up to 10 pounds: Over 2/3 of the time; up to 25 pounds: Up to 2/3 of the time; up to 50 pounds: Under 1/3 of the time. This position has the following special vision requirements: • Close vision (clear vision at 20 inches or less). • Distance vision (clear vision at 20 feet or more). • Color vision (ability to identify and distinquish colors). • Depth perception (three-dimensional vision, ability to judge distances and spatial relationships). • Ability to adjust focus (ability to adjust the eye to bring an object into sharp focus). • Peripheral vision (ability to observe an area that can be seen up or down or to the left and right when vision is fixed on a given point). Open Date 08/30/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10499 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10537": {
      "title": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal |  FSC Peer Tutor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FSC Peer Tutor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title FSC Peer Tutor Department Falcon Success Center Tutoring Program Rate of Pay $9 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Jobship and Work-Study General Description Provide students with individual and group tutoring services. Peer tutors may be hired from this posting throughout the 2025-2026 academic year. Essential Job Duties Provide students with individual and group tutoring services. Tutor students in both face-to-face and online contexts as needed. Coach students to become independent and confident learners by helping them improve study habits and skills. Provide an encouraging environment for students to learn. Peer tutors must be able to perform essential duties with or without reasonable accommodations. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent. Must have completed a minimum of one semester of college coursework, preferably at UM. Must have previously completed the course(s) you wish to tutor and earned a final grade of “A” in the course(s). Must have and maintain a minimum overall GPA of 3.0. Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Must have strong interpersonal communication skills to assess needs of clients and make plans of action to address their academic needs. Possess good study habits. Acumen to teach and desire to help others. Must be reliable and punctual. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 05/10/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Letter of Application University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10536": {
      "title": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Peer Academic Coaches Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Peer Academic Coaches Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Peer Academic Coaches Department Falcon Success Center Rate of Pay $8.50 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Jobship and Work-Study General Description Peer coaches will help students: Identify and use appropriate campus services; Become familiar with academic policies; Work on improving time management to avoid and/or overcome procrastination; Set and maintain academic goals; Organize class materials and prepare for assignments and exams; Build self-confidence; Adopt accountability strategies. Essential Job Duties -Establish and maintain interpersonal relationships with peers focusing on helping new students make a smooth transition, acclimate to campus, and establish a sense of belonging; -Make weekly contact with mentees; -Assist with workshops as requested by the Student Success Coach ( SSC ); -Assist students in meeting academic expectations (attendance, grades, conduct, and accountability); -Maintain confidentiality with peer’s personal information, such as contact information, issues, or problems; -Determine conflict resolutions and understand when to seek advice and guidance from the SSC ; -Be considerate, courteous, friendly, and cooperative with fellow peers, staff, and mentees; -Participate in mentor trainings and workshops assigned by the SSC ; -Meet regularly with the SSC to set goals and review progress of meeting those goals; -Conduct and lead weekly accountability groups consisting of 6-8 students. Education and Experience Sophomore, Junior, or Senior. Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities -Must be enrolled as a student at the University of Montevallo; -Passed English 101 and English 102 with at least a B; -Has a UM institutional GPA of 2.75 or higher; -Must possess strong oral and written communication skills; -Desire to help students succeed; -Have not had any student conduct referrals in the past year (previous 2 semesters). Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 05/09/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
