    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10555": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting (Taxation)",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Accounting (Taxation) - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Accounting (Taxation) - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500151 Job Title Assistant Professor of Accounting (Taxation) - Tenure Track Position Number F50300 Salary Commensurate with experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Tenure Track General Description The Michael E. Stephens College of Business ( SCOB ) at the University of Montevallo seeks a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Accounting. The anticipated start date is January 2027, although candidates who are unable to begin in January may be considered for an August 2027 start. Essential Job Duties Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate accounting and MBA courses, along with enthusiasm for scholarly engagement and mentorship of students from diverse academic and career backgrounds. Preference will be given to candidates with the ability to teach tax accounting. Additional Duties Strong communication skills; a substantive commitment to excellence in teaching taxation and other undergraduate accounting courses with students from a wide array of academic and career backgrounds, as well as the ability and willingness to teach MBA courses. Demonstrated ability or potential to engage in scholarly and research activities consistent with AACSB standards and the expectations of the University. Education and Experience A Ph.D. in Accounting from an AACSB -accredited institution is required. However, ABD doctoral candidates nearing completion will also be considered. Preferred Education and Experience Special consideration will also be given to applicants with professional certifications (e.g., CPA , CMA ) or relevant industry experience. Licenses, Certification or Registrations CPA License preferred. Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 8/15/2027 Open Date 09/12/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Assistant Professor of Accounting– Tenure Track Position: The Michael E. Stephens College of Business ( SCOB ) at the University of Montevallo seeks a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Accounting. The anticipated start date is January 2027, although candidates who are unable to begin in January may be considered for an August 2027 start. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate accounting and MBA courses, along with enthusiasm for scholarly engagement and mentorship of students from diverse academic and career backgrounds. Preference will be given to candidates with the ability to teach tax accounting. Overview of the Stephens College of Business: The SCOB Department of Business supports undergraduate programs in General Business, Data Analytics, Management, Marketing, Finance, and Accounting as well as a Master’s in Business Administration. These programs are fully accredited through the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business ( AACSB ). The average class size in SCOB is 21 students, underscoring our commitment to individualized learning. Instructors may teach up to 15 credit hours per semester. Our Campus: The University of Montevallo is Alabama’s only public liberal arts institution. Located approximately 30 miles South of Birmingham, Alabama. The University of Montevallo (UM) serves approximately 2,900 students annually. Montevallo offers undergraduate and graduate programs across the Colleges of Arts & Sciences, Business, Education and Human Development, Fine Arts, and Health Professions. SCOB currently supports approximately 385 undergraduate and 35 graduate students. Across the five Colleges, UM offers bachelors, masters, educational specialist, and doctoral degrees. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Accounting from an AACSB -accredited institution is required. However, ABD doctoral candidates nearing completion will also be considered. Strong communication skills; a substantive commitment to excellence in teaching taxation and other undergraduate accounting courses with students from a wide array of academic and career backgrounds, as well as the ability and willingness to teach MBA courses. Demonstrated ability or potential to engage in scholarly and research activities consistent with AACSB standards and the expectations of the University. Desired Qualifications: Special consideration will also be given to applicants with professional certifications (e.g., CPA , CMA ) or relevant industry experience. To Apply: Nominations and inquiries should be directed to Search Committee Chair, Dr. Milad Jasemi, at mjasemiz@montevallo.edu . Applicants should apply online at https://jobs.montevallo.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10534 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy References Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10556": {
      "title": "Full-Time Economics Instructor (Non-Tenure Track)",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Full-Time Economics Instructor (Non-Tenure Track) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Full-Time Economics Instructor (Non-Tenure Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500150 Job Title Full-Time Economics Instructor (Non-Tenure Track) Position Number F02281 Salary Commensurate with experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Non Tenure Track General Description The Michael E. Stephens College of Business ( SCOB ) at the University of Montevallo seeks an Instructor to teach undergraduate courses in Economics, beginning August 2027. This is a full-time, non-tenure track position. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in economics and university and professional service. Teaching assignments may include day, evening, or online courses. Essential Job Duties Dedicated teacher, active scholar and effective mentor for students with diverse backgrounds, preparation and career goals. Additional Duties Education and Experience Masters degree in Economics or a closely related field from an AACSB -accredited institution; strong communication skills; a substantive commitment to excellence in teaching undergraduate economics courses with students from a wide array of academic and career backgrounds. Preferred Education and Experience Experience teaching Microeconomics and Macroeconomics Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 8/15/2027 Open Date 09/12/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Instructor-Economics Position: The Michael E. Stephens College of Business ( SCOB ) at the University of Montevallo seeks an Instructor to teach undergraduate courses in Economics, beginning August 2027. This is a full-time, non-tenure track position. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in economics and university and professional service. Teaching assignments may include day, evening, or online courses. Overview of the Stephens College of Business: The SCOB Department of Business supports undergraduate programs in General Business, Data Analytics, Management, Marketing, Finance, and Accounting as well as a Master’s in Business Administration. These programs are fully accredited through the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business ( AACSB ). The average class size in SCOB is 21 students, underscoring our commitment to individualized learning. Instructors may teach up to 15 credit hours per semester. Our Campus: The University of Montevallo is Alabama’s only public liberal arts institution. Located approximately 30 miles South of Birmingham, Alabama, the University of Montevallo (UM) serves approximately 2,900 students annually. Montevallo offers undergraduate and graduate programs across the Colleges of Arts & Sciences, Business, Education and Human Development, Fine Arts, and Health Professions. SCOB currently supports approximately 385 undergraduate and 35 graduate students. Across the five Colleges, UM offers bachelors, masters, educational specialist, and doctoral degrees. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Masters degree in Economics or a closely related field from an AACSB -accredited institution; strong communication skills; a substantive commitment to excellence in teaching undergraduate economics courses with students from a wide array of academic and career backgrounds. Desired Qualifications: Documented experience and excellence in teaching; experience or research activity qualifying the candidate for one of the four categories needed for AACSB qualification. To Apply: Nominations and inquiries should be directed to Search Committee Chair, Dr. Milad Jasemi, at mjasemiz@montevallo.edu . Applicants should apply online at https://jobs.montevallo.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10533 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy References Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10562": {
      "title": "Student Office Assistant, Social Work and Speech Pathology",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Student Office Assistant, Social Work and Speech Pathology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Office Assistant, Social Work and Speech Pathology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Student Office Assistant, Social Work and Speech Pathology Department Social Work and Speech Pathology Rate of Pay $8 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Jobship and Work-Study General Description Perform general office and receptionist duties for the Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology. Essential Job Duties 1) Provide friendly and helpful customer service by welcoming and assisting visitors & clients, answering & directing phone calls, and taking messages. 2) Sort and distribute mail. 3) Assist faculty & staff with tasks as needed. 4) Sort and file clinic related paperwork. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 1) Be self-directed and motivated. 2) Great attitude and interpersonal skills. 3) Ability to multitask. 4) Possess good phone skills; including pleasant manner and ability to take & relay accurate messages. 5) Be able to adhere to HIPPA guidelines. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations none Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 10/02/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Class Schedule Optional Documents Letter of Application Resume University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
