    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10574": {
      "title": "Chemical Science Specialist, Alabama Science in Motion program (ASIM),",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Chemical Science Specialist, Alabama Science in Motion program (ASIM), Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Chemical Science Specialist, Alabama Science in Motion program (ASIM), Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S1500773 Job Title Chemical Science Specialist, Alabama Science in Motion program (ASIM), Position Number P80093 Division Academic Affairs/Provost - ACA Department Alabama Math Science and Technology Initiative (AMSTI) FLSA Exempt Salary Grade based on state salary matrix Salary Classification Admin/Professional Annual Salary Range Hourly Salary Range Employment Status Full Time 11 Mos Regular General Description AMSTI is the Alabama State Department of Education’s ( ALSDE ) initiative to improve STEM education in Alabama so that all students develop the skills necessary for success in post-secondary studies and the workforce. Established in 1994, ASIM now serves as the secondary science component of AMSTI . ASIM /Secondary Science Specialists support schools by providing professional learning, instructional materials, and educator support (through coaching) needed to implement the current Alabama Course of Study Standards: Science in grades 6-12 (including but not limited to biology, chemistry, and/or physics). Regional assignments (schools/districts and grade levels/content areas) will be based on regional needs and are subject to change based on regional data. Essential Job Duties PROFESSIONAL LEARNING : 1. Facilitate and/or participate in professional learning for teachers and/or administrators based on assignments and/or LEA needs, including online options. 2. Assist AMSTI - ALSDE in developing and maintaining common professional learning offerings and supporting resources for AMSTI and/or for the ALSDE , including online options. 3. Provide ongoing professional learning to AMSTI lead teachers, certified AMSTI facilitators, and/or instructional coaches. 4. Assist IHEs with planning and conducting pre-service and continuing education/outreach activities. 5. Participate in AMSTI professional learning activities and staff meetings conducted by the ALSDE and Site Director, unless prior approval for absence is granted. EDUCATOR SUPPORT : 6. Provide frequent, ongoing support and coaching to teachers, AMSTI lead teachers, certified AMSTI facilitators, instructional coaches, and/or administrators based on assignments and/or LEA needs as defined annually based on data. 7. Assist AMSTI teachers in effectively using common planning time and Professional Learning Communities to improve instruction. 8. Assist in recruiting new AMSTI teachers and/or facilitators. 9. Conduct research on the effects of current math, science, and/or technology practices in AMSTI classrooms, as requested by the ALSDE . 10. Coordinate work through the AMSTI Site Director, collaborate with other specialists, and communicate with all stakeholders. 11. Achieve and maintain proficiency in all standards, pedagogical content knowledge, and AMSTI lessons and practices through AMSTI - ALSDE and approved outside professional learning opportunities, based on the AMSTI requirements. INSTRUCTIONAL MATERIALS : 12. Work with materials managers to make site-level decisions based on teacher needs/requests. ○ Some preparation, delivery, pick up, and maintenance of lesson materials and equipment may be required, including lifting (up to 50 pounds) and driving (box truck or delivery van) 13. Provide feedback to the ALSDE regarding the customization of kits and materials to make them teacher/classroom-friendly. GENERAL DUTIES : 14. Maintain records (including financial) and complete paperwork in a timely manner. 15. Participate in the development, maintenance, and promotion of AMSTI resources according to the resource development and PR requirements. 16. Communicate with AMSTI Site Director and ALSDE in advance as it pertains to retirement or resignation plans (under normal circumstances, a minimum of six-month advance notice is requested) 17. ASIM / Secondary Science Specialist responsibilities include but are not limited to those listed in all categories above; specialists may be required to perform other duties as assigned by the AMSTI Site Director or AMSTI - ALSDE , including overnight travel. Additional Duties Essential Job Duties are intended to be examples of duties and are not intended to be all-inclusive. There will be other duties as assigned. The individual holding this position will serve as a representative of the University and, as such, shall promote a positive impression by demonstrating a collegial and professional customer-service approach at all times. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of and experience with AMSTI or ASIM program preferred. Demonstrated competence in oral and written communication Education and Experience Minimum of six (6) years of teaching experience in an Alabama public middle and/or high school required. Master’s degree (preferred) from a regionally accredited college or university (preferred science or science education) Experience providing professional development for teachers preferred. Teacher leader or instructional coaching experience preferred. Licenses, Certification or Registrations Valid Alabama Teachers’ Certification in Secondary Science required (general science preferred) Current Alabama driver’s license and acceptable driving record required Environmental Working Conditions Indoor Travel Requirements Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Physical Requirements Ability to lift heavy objects (at or below 40 pounds) required. Transport of science equipment and laboratory supplies to area schools. Open Date 10/02/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10565 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
