    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10575": {
      "title": "Part-Time Counselor",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Part-Time Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S1500772 Job Title Part-Time Counselor Position Number P12534 Division Student Affairs Department Counseling Services Department FLSA Non-Exempt Salary Grade Salary Classification Admin/Professional Annual Salary Range Hourly Salary Range Up to $35 per hour (based on experience) Employment Status Part Time 12 Mos Regular General Description The purpose of this position is to provide direct mental health counseling and crisis management to members of the campus community. Essential Job Duties Provide clinical services to UM Clients (students, faculty, and staff). Services include, but are not limited to, intake assessments, individual follow-up, crisis intervention, and case management. Serve as a point of contact and provide consultation to faculty, staff, parents, and students expressing concerns regarding members of the University community exhibiting signs of distress. Prepare and maintain appropriate clinical and non-clinical documentation for University clients within departmental deadlines. Maintain ethical, legal, and best practice standards of care consistent with applicable state and federal laws, UM Policies and Procedures, CS Operating Procedures, applicable code of the ethics ( ACA ). Consult with CS Director about high risk clients and attend weekly clinical staffing. Continue professional development through active memberships, presentations, and conference/training events to ensure adherence to best practices. Promote and maintain positive relationships across the UM campus and community by working effectively with on and off campus partners. Serve on assigned Student Affairs and University committees. Assist with University and Division of Enrollment and Student Affairs events/activities as needed and requested. Assume other duties as the Counseling Services Director may assign. Additional Duties Essential Job Duties are intended to be examples of duties and are not intended to be all inclusive. There will be other duties as assigned. The individual holding this position will serve as a representative of the University and, as such, shall promote a positive impression by demonstrating a collegial and professional customer-service approach at all times. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to maintain a strict level of confidentiality in performing duties. Working knowledge of FERPA , Title IX, VAWA , and applicable confidentiality laws. Knowledge of counseling techniques, ethical codes, and best practices. Ability to manage crisis situations effectively. Ability to work comfortably with diverse populations. Understanding of human development and college student development. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to manage large volume of information with a high degree of accuracy and detail. Must be self-directed and able to complete projects with limited supervision. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Outlook, Excel, and PowerPoint). Ability to learn and effectively use other software platforms (i.e. Titanium Scheduler, Banner, Maxient) utilized by the department. Ability to work as a contributing member of the CS team. Education and Experience Master’s Degree in Counseling, Social Work, or related field. No experience necessary. One to two years of experience working with distressed individuals in a higher education setting preferred. Licenses, Certification or Registrations Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications required for this position include: None Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications preferred for this position include: Eligible for licensure in the state of Alabama. Environmental Working Conditions Indoor Travel Requirements Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Physical Requirements Open Date 10/02/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10564 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10572": {
      "title": "Instructor of Technical Direction",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Instructor of Technical Direction Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor of Technical Direction Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Additional materials may be requested in later rounds of the application process. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500152 Job Title Instructor of Technical Direction Position Number F70227 Salary Competitive with Market FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Non Tenure Track General Description The University of Montevallo’s College of Fine Arts invites applicants for a full-time Instructor in Technical Direction beginning Fall 2027. The ideal candidate should be proficient in theatrical building techniques, woodworking, welding, rigging, and computer aided drafting, and possess strong project management and leadership skills. The Technical Director should have expertise in traditional craft and contemporary entertainment technology. The primary teaching responsibilities of this position are Stagecraft I, Stagecraft II, Theatre Practicum, and/or other courses based on departmental needs and areas of specialty. Essential Job Duties Teach and mentor students in hands on construction. Set and enforce best safety practices and set safe-use guidelines for use of all equipment and tools. Oversee the construction and installation of all technical elements for assigned productions, ensuring they are built to design specifications, within budget, and on schedule, while maintaining the highest standards of safety and craftsmanship. Oversee the strike of all technical elements for the Theatre program’s season. Daily operation, organization, and management of the scene shop. Coordinate all technical needs for the Theatre program. Communicate theatrical inventory and maintenance needs to the Director of Operations for the Alan and Lindsey Song Center for the Arts. Create build schedules for each Theatre production. Attend all technical rehearsals for productions. Supervise student and work study crews to build scenic elements. Advise production managers, directors, and designers on feasibility, cost, and equipment capabilities. Attend all Theatre program production meetings. Develop technical drafts from designer drawings. Participate in Theatre program recruitment activities. Additional Duties Education and Experience Master’s degree in Theatre or a related field. Teaching experience at the collegiate level or significant and clearly demonstrated professional experience in instruction and/or mentoring. Professional theatrical production experience . Preferred Education and Experience MFA in Technical Direction or related field. Experience in sound Experience in Qlab Proficiency in Vectorworks Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 10/01/2026 Close Date 11/15/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Additional materials may be requested in later rounds of the application process. Additional Information Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10552 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application References Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10588": {
      "title": "Open-Rank, Tenure-Track Faculty in Counseling",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Open-Rank, Tenure-Track Faculty in Counseling – Director, Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Open-Rank, Tenure-Track Faculty in Counseling – Director, Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500149 Job Title Open-Rank, Tenure-Track Faculty in Counseling – Director, Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic Position Number TBD Salary Commensurate with experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Tenure Track General Description The University of Montevallo invites applications for an open-rank, tenure-track faculty position in Counseling. The successful candidate will teach in the Graduate Counseling Program and serve as Director of the Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic, the program’s on-campus training clinic. Responsibilities include teaching graduate counseling courses, providing leadership and oversight of clinic operations, providing site supervision to practicum and internship students completing clinical experiences within the clinic, supervising graduate assistants assigned to the clinic, and coordinating clinic-related community outreach initiatives. The position carries a 2/2 teaching load in recognition of the faculty member’s assigned Clinic Director and clinical supervision responsibilities. The faculty member will also receive a separate contract for clinic operations during the summer outside of the 9-month base contract period. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Essential Job Duties Teach graduate-level courses in the Counseling Program with a 2/2 course load, reflecting assigned responsibilities as Director of the program’s on-campus training clinic. Serve as Director of the Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic and provide leadership and oversight of the clinic’s operations, clinical training activities, and community services. Provide site supervision for practicum and internship students completing clinical experiences within the Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic, consistent with program, university, accreditation, and professional standards. Supervise graduate assistants assigned to the Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic. Provide academic advising and mentorship to graduate students in the Counseling Program. Maintain an active program of scholarship, including peer-reviewed publications and professional presentations. Maintain an active professional counseling identity through engagement in relevant professional organizations and activities. Participate in recruitment, retention, and other initiatives that support the continued growth and success of the Counseling Program. Serve on department, college, and university committees and contribute service to the counseling profession and broader community. Perform other duties consistent with the faculty role and the needs of the Counseling Program. Additional Duties Perform other duties as assigned that are consistent with the faculty member’s role, academic appointment, and responsibilities within the Counseling Program and Grainger Community Counseling and Wellness Clinic. Participate in additional program, department, college, or university initiatives as appropriate to the faculty role. Education and Experience Doctorate in Counselor Education from a CACREP -accredited program (or related doctoral degree with one full-time faculty year before July 1, 2013). · Demonstrated professional identity and active engagement in the counseling profession, including at least two of the following: Participation in counseling-related continuing education, conferences, workshops, or other professional development activities. Professional service, leadership, or advocacy in counseling. Ongoing clinical practice or clinical supervision. Research, scholarship, presentations, or publications in counseling or counselor education. Preferred Education and Experience Graduate-level teaching experience in counseling or counselor education. · Experience with the administration, coordination, or operation of a university-based counseling training clinic or comparable clinical training environment. · Experience supervising and supporting the clinical development of graduate counseling students. Experience with CACREP -accredited counseling programs and clinical training standards. · Supervision-related credentials (e.g., LPC -S, LMFT -S, ACS ) or equivalent state-recognized supervision credential. Licenses, Certification or Registrations Candidates must hold and maintain an active, independent professional license in counseling or marriage and family therapy (e.g., LPC , LMFT , or equivalent) in a U.S. state or jurisdiction. Candidates must maintain appropriate professional licensure throughout their appointment consistent with accreditation requirements and assigned clinical supervision responsibilities. Eligibility for licensure as an LPC or LMFT in Alabama is preferred. Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Open Date 09/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information Required documents: Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application Other document: Proof of License Unofficial Transcripts Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10510 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application Other Document Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10592": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor of Instructional Leadership-Tenure Track",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Open Rank Professor of Instructional Leadership-Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Professor of Instructional Leadership-Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500154 Job Title Open Rank Professor of Instructional Leadership-Tenure Track Position Number TBD Salary Commensurate with experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Tenure Track General Description The Department of Teaching, Leadership, and Technology in the College of Education and Human Development ( CEHD ) at the University of Montevallo invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Open Rank Professor of Instructional Leadership , beginning August 2027. We welcome applications from candidates qualified for appointment at the Assistant, Associate, or Professor level. Essential Job Duties The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty team preparing practicing educators and educational leaders across master’s, specialist, and doctoral programs. The position offers opportunities to: teach and mentor students across multiple graduate pathways; contribute to a growing doctoral program serving practicing educational leaders; mentor scholar-practitioners conducting applied dissertation research; design and teach innovative graduate courses in synchronous and asynchronous online formats; strengthen the quality, growth, and continuous improvement of the College’s instructional leadership programs; engage in applied scholarship addressing educational problems of practice; and build meaningful partnerships with P–12 schools, school districts, educational organizations, and communities. The College seeks a colleague who will contribute intellectually and collaboratively to its instructional leadership programs and prepare reflective, ethical educational leaders who use evidence to guide meaningful improvement in schools and communities. Additional Duties Overview of the Department of Teaching, Leadership, and Technology ( TLT ) : TLT supports undergraduate and graduate educator preparation in Elementary Education, Elementary/Collaborative Education, Education of the Deaf and Hard of Hearing, and Secondary Education, along with advanced programs in Instructional Leadership, Curriculum and Teacher Development, and Instructional Technology. Programs integrate coursework, clinical experiences, technology, and applied research to prepare educators and educational leaders. Faculty collaborate with school partners to connect academic preparation with professional practice and support students through advising, supervision, and feedback. The Instructional Leadership program includes master’s, specialist, and doctoral-level preparation and serves practicing educators and leaders through flexible online and blended formats. This position offers an opportunity to contribute to a growing doctoral program and a comprehensive instructional leadership program that prepares scholar-practitioners to address educational problems of practice through evidence-informed leadership, inquiry, and continuous improvement. Education and Experience Required Qualifications: An earned doctorate in instructional leadership, educational administration, educational leadership, education policy, or a closely related field by the date of appointment. Minimum of three years of experience in P–12 educational leadership, such as principal, assistant principal, district-level administrator, central office administrator, assistant superintendent, superintendent, or a closely related leadership role. Evidence of potential for or an established record of effective teaching in higher education, commensurate with rank. Evidence of potential for or an established record of scholarly activity, commensurate with rank. Demonstrated commitment to graduate student advising, mentoring, and professional preparation. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and educational partners from diverse backgrounds and professional contexts. . Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Education and Experience: Preference may be given to candidates with one or more of the following: Experience teaching and/or developing graduate courses in instructional leadership or educational administration. Experience teaching in asynchronous, synchronous, or blended online learning environments. Experience chairing or serving on doctoral dissertation committees. Expertise in one or more areas such as ethics, school finance, school law, strategic planning, or related areas. A record of applied scholarship that connects research to educational leadership practice. Licenses, Certification or Registrations NA Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 8/15/2027 Open Date 10/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information FULL ADVERTISEMENT : Open Rank Professor of Instructional Leadership-Tenure Track Position: The Department of Teaching, Leadership, and Technology in the College of Education and Human Development ( CEHD ) at the University of Montevallo invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Open Rank Professor of Instructional Leadership , beginning August 2027. We welcome applications from candidates qualified for appointment at the Assistant, Associate, or Professor level. The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty team preparing practicing educators and educational leaders across master’s, specialist, and doctoral programs. The position offers opportunities to: •        teach and mentor students across multiple graduate pathways; •        contribute to a growing doctoral program serving practicing educational leaders; •        mentor scholar-practitioners conducting applied dissertation research; •        design and teach innovative graduate courses in synchronous and asynchronous online formats; •        strengthen the quality, growth, and continuous improvement of the College’s instructional leadership programs; •        engage in applied scholarship addressing educational problems of practice; and •        build meaningful partnerships with P–12 schools, school districts, educational organizations, and communities. The College seeks a colleague who will contribute intellectually and collaboratively to its instructional leadership programs and prepare reflective, ethical educational leaders who use evidence to guide meaningful improvement in schools and communities. Overview of the Department of Teaching, Leadership, and Technology ( TLT ) : TLT supports undergraduate and graduate educator preparation in Elementary Education, Elementary/Collaborative Education, Education of the Deaf and Hard of Hearing, and Secondary Education, along with advanced programs in Instructional Leadership, Curriculum and Teacher Development, and Instructional Technology. Programs integrate coursework, clinical experiences, technology, and applied research to prepare educators and educational leaders. Faculty collaborate with school partners to connect academic preparation with professional practice and support students through advising, supervision, and feedback. The Instructional Leadership program includes master’s, specialist, and doctoral-level preparation and serves practicing educators and leaders through flexible online and blended formats. This position offers an opportunity to contribute to a growing doctoral program and a comprehensive instructional leadership program that prepares scholar-practitioners to address educational problems of practice through evidence-informed leadership, inquiry, and continuous improvement. Our Campus: The University of Montevallo is Alabama’s only public liberal arts institution. Located approximately 30 miles South of Birmingham, Alabama–Alabama’s largest metropolitan area. The University of Montevallo (UM) serves approximately 2,900 students annually. Montevallo offers undergraduate and graduate programs across the Colleges of Arts & Sciences, Business, Education and Human Development, Fine Arts, and Health Professions. In addition, UM’s liberal arts atmosphere fosters collaborative teaching and other academic endeavors. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: • An earned doctorate in instructional leadership, educational administration, educational leadership, education policy, or a closely related field by the date of appointment. • Minimum of three years of experience in P–12 educational leadership, such as principal, assistant principal, district-level administrator, central office administrator, assistant superintendent, superintendent, or a closely related leadership role. • Evidence of potential for or an established record of effective teaching in higher education, commensurate with rank. • Evidence of potential for or an established record of scholarly activity, commensurate with rank. • Demonstrated commitment to graduate student advising, mentoring, and professional preparation. • Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and educational partners from diverse backgrounds and professional contexts. Preferred Education and Experience: Preference may be given to candidates with one or more of the following: • Experience teaching and/or developing graduate courses in instructional leadership or educational administration. • Experience teaching in asynchronous, synchronous, or blended online learning environments. • Experience chairing or serving on doctoral dissertation committees. • Expertise in one or more areas such as ethics, school finance, school law, strategic planning, or related areas. • A record of applied scholarship that connects research to educational leadership practice. Rank: Rank will be determined based on the candidate’s qualifications, professional experience, teaching record, scholarly accomplishments, service, and evidence of contributions appropriate to the University’s criteria for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. Candidates appointed at the Associate Professor or Professor level must demonstrate a record of accomplishments commensurate with the University’s expectations for tenure and promotion at the applicable rank. To Apply: Nominations and inquiries should be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Amy Samuels at asamuels@montevallo.edu . Applicants should apply online at https://jobs.montevallo.edu . Official transcripts will be required at interview in addition to three reference letters from individuals familiar with the applicant’s work. Review of applications will begin November 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10583 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10587": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Counseling (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, Counseling (Tenure-Track) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor, Counseling (Tenure-Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500148 Job Title Assistant Professor, Counseling (Tenure-Track) Position Number TBD Salary Commensurate with experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Tenure Track General Description The University of Montevallo invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Counseling position specializing in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. This faculty member will contribute to our CACREP -accredited program by teaching, supervising, conducting research, and engaging in service to the university and profession. Essential Job Duties Teach graduate-level courses in core CACREP and Clinical Mental Health Counseling specialization areas. · Provide academic advising to graduate students. · Supervise graduate student field placements (practicum/internship). · Maintain an independent research agenda and engage in scholarly activities (e.g., publish in peer-reviewed journals, deliver professional presentations). · Engage in professional counseling organizations and demonstrate active professional identity (e.g., ACA , AMHCA , ALCA ). · Actively recruit graduate students and contribute to program growth. · Serve on university, college, and department committees and contribute to the broader counseling community. Additional Duties Education and Experience Doctorate in Counselor Education from a CACREP -accredited program (or related doctoral degree with one full-time faculty year before July 1, 2013). · University-level teaching experience in counseling. · Education and clinical experience in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. · Active professional engagement, including at least two of the following: Professional development in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. Professional service/advocacy in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. Ongoing clinical practice. Research/scholarly activity in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. · Professional counseling identity demonstrated through: o Membership in national and state counseling organizations (e.g., ACA , AMHCA , ALCA ). Relevant professional credentials (e.g., LPC , NCC ). Preferred Education and Experience Established research agenda in counselor education. Experience in securing external funding for academic research. Demonstrated leadership in graduate counseling education. Licenses, Certification or Registrations Candidates must hold or be eligible for counseling licensure as an LPC in Alabama within 18 months of hire. Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Open Date 09/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information Required documents: Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application Other document: Proof of License Unofficial Transcripts Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10508 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae or Resume Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10589": {
      "title": "Tutoring Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Tutoring Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Tutoring Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S1500764 Job Title Tutoring Coordinator Position Number P41408 Division Academic Affairs/Provost - ACA Department Falcon Success Center FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 207 Salary Classification Admin/Professional Annual Salary Range $32,798 - $44,929 Hourly Salary Range Employment Status Full Time 12 Mos Regular General Description The purpose of this position is to coordinate tutoring services in subject areas as needed for students at the University of Montevallo. The tutoring coordinator in the Falcon Success Center ( FSC ) is responsible for recruiting, hiring, training, coordinating, and supervising quality tutors and services for academic success. Essential Job Duties Identify subject areas where there is a need for tutoring Collaborate with faculty and staff to recruit potential peer tutors Hire, train, supervise, and evaluate peer tutors who tutor in a variety of academic subjects and on a variety of topics such as note-taking, test preparation, time management, etc. that are identified through broad-based needs assessment Schedule peer tutors (one-on-one tutoring, group tutoring, and drop-in tutoring) both online and in-person Perform observations and write formal evaluations of peer tutors each semester Staff FSC front desk; train and supervise student assistants Manage and approve payroll for student staff Create and enforce policies for student staff at the FSC Manage the Center’s appointment management software Track tutoring data and compile reports each semester Conduct outcomes assessment and use results to make continuous improvements to tutoring services Serve as co-advisor for Alpha Lambda Delta, the honor society for first-year academic success Attend preview days, orientation days, and other events as required to advertise tutoring services to current and prospective UM students Create and conduct classroom presentations to introduce students to the academic services provided in the Center Engage in appropriate professional development opportunities Other duties as assigned Additional Duties Essential Job Duties are intended to be examples of duties and are not intended to be all inclusive. There will be other duties as assigned. The individual holding this position will serve as a representative of the University and, as such, shall promote a positive impression by demonstrating a collegial and professional customer-service approach at all times. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Excellent interpersonal and communication skills; Ability to work with students of all learning levels; Knowledge of learning strategies, study skills, and effective academic achievement strategies. Education and Experience The educational requirement for this position is: a Bachelor’s Degree Education substituted for experience? No This position requires one year of related experience in academic success or tutoring in higher education. Experience substituted for education? No Licenses, Certification or Registrations Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications required for this position include: • None Environmental Working Conditions Indoor Travel Requirements Light Travel Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Physical Requirements The physical activities required for this position involve: standing: Under 1/3 of the time walking: : Under 1/3 of the time sitting: Over 1/3 of the time using hands: Over 1/3 of the time reaching with hands and arms: Over 1/3 of the time climbing or balancing: Under 1/3 of the time stooping, kneeling, crouching, or crawling: : Under 1/3 of time talking or hearing: Over 1/3 of the time tasting or smelling: Never This position requires lifting: up to 10 pounds: Under 1/3 of the time up to 25 pounds: Under 1/3 of the time up to 50 pounds: Under 1/3 of the time up to 100 pounds: Never more than 100 pounds: Never Open Date 07/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10429 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
