    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10595": {
      "title": "Warehouse Foreman",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Warehouse Foreman Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Warehouse Foreman Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S1500775 Job Title Warehouse Foreman Position Number O01270 Division President - PRS Department Central Receiving and Mail Services FLSA Non-Exempt Salary Grade 110 Salary Classification Classified Annual Salary Range Hourly Salary Range $13.51 - $18.01 Employment Status Full Time 12 Mos Regular General Description The purpose of this position is to oversee the safe receipt, storage, retrieval and timely dispatch of goods. Perform technical and physical duties in securing control of all parts, supplies and materials in the Central Receiving warehouse. Essential Job Duties Audit physical inventory as required by policy; reconcile inventory records for accuracy in deterring theft and misuse; Implement and maintain programs to reduce shrinkage from warehouse; Assist with movable inventory; Order stock items for warehouse; Supervise, train and evaluate student assistants; prepare schedules and approve time sheets; Prepares and maintains proper documentation of deliveries from various customers; operates forklift and scissor lift to load/unloads materials and finished goods; Assures efficient distribution of supplies and materials within the warehouse and assists with set-up operations accordingly; Operate electronic inventory scanner to receive and log incoming items, and verify the accuracy of incoming shipments; Distributes materials, tools, or other stock items to fill requests using work orders and the inventory system; Maintain inventory of all supplies; assist with set up, monitor and maintain item inventory control systems including generating barcode labels, labeling products in warehouse, and using scanner to issue products as requested; Provides material handling activities necessary to bring material from the warehouse or prepare finished goods for shipping; Assists with the implementation of quality control measures for all aspects of warehouse; Assists with parcel shipping and receiving activities; assuring proper distribution of materials and signs off on behalf of the University accepting shipment of goods; Sort and store materials on racks, shelves, or in bins according to predetermined sequence such as size, type, color, or product code; label materials with identifying information; Perform regular inventory checks of tools and supplies to ensure stock is updated and accurate; Coordinates and maintain departmental package delivery schedules; Seek to achieve assigned departmental goals and objectives; Respond to customers via email, fax, and telephone; Record and maintain daily and weekly warehouse accounts for shops in the Physical Plant; Follow all university safety and accident procedures while on University premises or operating university vehicles or equipment; Perform basic housekeeping and maintenance of warehouse and equipment; Ensure that health and safety requirements are met and ensure the security of the building and stock; Receive, and tracks deliveries from UPS , FED -EX, and LTL (freight); Manage University electronic equipment and bulb & battery recycling program; Attends staff meetings and prescribed in-service training programs as needed; perform related duties as assigned. Additional Duties Essential Job Duties are intended to be examples of duties and are not intended to be all inclusive. There will be other duties as assigned. The individual holding this position will serve as a representative of the University and, as such, shall promote a positive impression by demonstrating a collegial and professional customer-service approach at all times. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to lift items weighing up to 50 lbs; Ability to operate a fork lift (daily) and scissor lift (occasionally); Strong communication and customer service skills; Strong interpersonal skills. Education and Experience The educational requirement for this position is: Completion of high school/ GED Education substituted for experience? Yes This position requires: 2 year of related experience. Experience substituted for education? Yes Licenses, Certification or Registrations Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications required for this position include: • Valid driver’s license • Acceptable driving record Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications preferred for this position include: Certified forklift operator preferred Environmental Working Conditions Indoor Travel Requirements None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Physical Requirements The physical activities required for this position involve: Standing: Up to 2/3 of the time; walking: Up to 2/3 of the time; sitting: Under 1/3 of the time; using hands: Up to 2/3 of the time; reaching with hands and arms: Up to 2/3 of the time; climbing or balancing: Under 1/3 of the time; stooping, kneeling, crouching, or crawling: Under 1/3 of the time; talking or hearing: Up to 2/3 of the time; and, tasting or smelling: Under 1/3 of the time. This position requires lifting: Up to 10 pounds: Up to 2/3 of the time; up to 25 pounds: Up to 2/3 of the time; up to 50 pounds: Under 1/3 of the time; up to 100 pounds: Under 1/3 of the time; and, more than 100 pounds: None of the time. This position has the following special vision requirements: • Close vision (clear vision at 20 inches or less). Open Date 10/22/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10591 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10598": {
      "title": "Open Rank, Instructor (Tenure or Non-tenure Track), Nursing",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Open Rank, Instructor (Tenure or Non-tenure Track), Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank, Instructor (Tenure or Non-tenure Track), Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500147 Job Title Open Rank, Instructor (Tenure or Non-tenure Track), Nursing Position Number TBD Salary Commensurate with experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Tenure or Non-Tenure Track General Description The University of Montevallo’s Department of Nursing and Health Sciences housed within the College of Health Professions invite applications for a nine-month, OOpen Rank, Instructor (Tenure or Non-tenure Track), Nursing. Assigned teaching responsibilities include undergraduate teaching with prelicensure students in the classroom, lab, and clinical settings. Specifically, the successful candidate will teach maternal child/reproductive health and/or nursing care of children as well as other nursing courses. Summer teaching may be required for this position and compensation will be provided. This position is designed for a dynamic nurse educator committed to excellence in teaching, student mentoring, and scholarly engagement. The successful candidate will participate in academic advising; curriculum development and program assessment; establish an independent line of scholarly activity/research and publish in scholarly journals; and provide service to the program, department, college, university, and community. Essential Job Duties Primary teaching responsibilities are in the undergraduate prelicensure track teaching maternal/child/reproductive health and/or nursing care of children and will include additional nursing courses (including the RN to BSN track courses) based on qualifications. Additional responsibilities include academic advising, scholarship/research, service to the program, department, college, university, and the community. Additional Duties Education and Experience Master’s degree in nursing required; Doctoral degree in nursing is preferred. Preferred Education and Experience Documented experience and excellence in teaching; peer-reviewed publications in translational, human subjects research; evidence of successful advising at the undergraduate level; simulation experience or certified healthcare simulation educator; membership and involvement in professional organizations; familiarity with the AACN Essentials and the Commission of Collegiate Nursing Education organizations. Licenses, Certification or Registrations Must possess an unencumbered registered nursing (RN) license in Alabama, multistate RN license, or be eligible for Alabama RN licensure prior to beginning employment. Maintains American Heart Association BLS HCP certification. Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Open Date 08/30/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10501 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Unofficial Transcripts Letter of Recommendation 1 Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10603": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor (Tenure-track) Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Assistant or Associate Professor (Tenure-track) Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant or Associate Professor (Tenure-track) Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application review begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500142 Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor (Tenure-track) Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology Position Number TBD Salary Commensurate with rank, qualifications, and experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Tenure Track General Description The University of Montevallo’s Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology housed within the College of Health Professions invites applications for a nine-month, tenure track position in Speech-Language Pathology at the level of Assistant or Associate Professor. Assigned teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate and graduate teaching, and clinical supervision and clinical teaching of speech-language pathology graduate students. Summer teaching and supervision opportunities may be available but are not required. This position is designed for a dynamic educator committed to excellence in teaching, student mentorship and supervision, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Teaching and supervision methods, practices, and strategies should be in accordance with current evidence and best practice guidelines. The successful candidate will contribute to the development and delivery of curriculum that prepares students for careers in speech language pathology. Essential Job Duties Responsibilities include graduate and undergraduate teaching, graduate clinical supervision, research, academic advising, and service to the department, college, and the University. Area of interest is open. UM offers the B.S. and M.S. in SLP through an accredited program. Additional Duties Education and Experience CCC - SLP and Ph.D./ SLP -D in Communication Sciences and Disorders or related field are required. Strong ADB candidates will be considered. Preferred Education and Experience Licenses, Certification or Registrations Current ASHA Certification, must be maintained Alabama State License or be eligible to obtain Alabama State Licensure prior to beginning employment, must be maintained Must possess or complete required supervisor-related training for speech language pathology Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date 08/15/2026 Open Date 04/13/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Application review begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Additional Information The Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology at the University of Montevallo is seeking a candidate for a nine-month, tenure track position in Speech-Language Pathology at the level of Assistant or Associate Professor. Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10250 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts References Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
